<section class="features" aria-labelledby="features-title">
  <header>
    <p>02 / Built for the route</p>
    <h2 id="features-title">Reliable transfer.<br /><em>Deliberate traffic.</em></h2>
  </header>
  <div class="feature-grid">
    <article>
      <p class="number">01</p><div>
        <h3>Persistent recovery</h3><p>
          Pause, resume, cancel, retry, and recover transfers across daemon restarts. Validators and
          partial state protect file integrity.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article>
      <p class="number">02</p><div>
        <h3>Intentional scheduling</h3><p>
          Bounded concurrency and stable high, normal, and low queue priorities keep parallel work
          predictable.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article>
      <p class="number">03</p><div>
        <h3>Network awareness</h3><p>
          NetworkManager state, metered-link behavior, and profiles adapt download decisions to the
          active connection.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="governance">
      <p class="number">04</p><div>
        <h3>Linux traffic governance</h3><p>
          An optional capability-limited helper coordinates cgroups, conntrack, nftables, IFB, and <code
            >tc</code
          > without making the downloader daemon root.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div
        class="policy-scale"
        aria-label="Available traffic policies: off, focus, balanced, throughput, latency"
      >
        <span>off</span><span>focus</span><span>balanced</span><span>throughput</span><span
          >latency</span
        >
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

